# Check out LF everywhere, on every machine.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) checks text
# files out with CRLF, and the Windows release leg breaks twice: the version
# check cannot parse the files it reads, and — silently — the build embeds the
# plugin's `#!/bin/sh` hook scripts byte for byte (include_str! in
# src-tauri/src/claude/hooks.rs), which sh then refuses to run. Gitweaver hit
# the same on the same desktop.
#
# `eol=lf` on the catch-all rather than a list of extensions, so a file type
# nobody listed (mc-hook and mc-wake have no extension at all) cannot come out
# CRLF on one machine. Nothing here needs CRLF: PowerShell, Node, Rust and git
# are all content with LF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never diff, never munge.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
